CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ empty pack: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ one element: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body of function
--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/5.2, /7: `struct impl2 : leaf<T>...' with T = <>
has no base.  An empty pack has no element list in the template map, only
its size, so the base-specifier was kept unexpanded, and every
constructor default-initialized the base `leaf<T>' ("found no match for
symbol 'leaf'"): the constructors of impl<int> and impl2<> were dropped
(bin53).  libc++'s __tuple_impl<__tuple_indices<>> has this shape.  g++
13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
